~ report.wit — a release note assembled from live external data.
~
~ Each `@load <alias> load@` names data that lives outside the document; a
~ program (wired in wit.sources.json) produces it at build time. `env` is a
~ built-in source — no config, no program — that exposes the environment.
~
~ Build (from the repo root):
~   node packages/cli/dist/bin.js build examples/load-demo/report.wit \
~     --sources examples/load-demo/wit.sources.json --allow-exec \
~     --env examples/load-demo/.env --fragment

@load meta load@
@load team load@
@load downloads load@
@load env load@

@h1 Release @meta.version h1@

Cut @meta.date on branch @env.WIT_BRANCH.

@h2 Contributors h2@
@ul
(each @team as person) @li @person.name — @person.commits commits li@ (end)
ul@

@h2 Downloads by platform h2@
~ a real CSV file (data/downloads.csv), read at build time and handed
~ straight to a table node — columns come from the header row, no schema.
@table |rows @downloads|

~ the same chart at every size preset — figures centre by default,
~ and |size| is small / medium / large / full (or a number / percent).
@figure
  @img |src assets/downloads.svg| |alt Chart, small| |size small|
  @figcaption size small — 220px figcaption@
figure@

@figure
  @img |src assets/downloads.svg| |alt Chart, medium| |size medium|
  @figcaption size medium — 380px figcaption@
figure@

@figure
  @img |src assets/downloads.svg| |alt Chart, large| |size large|
  @figcaption size large — 600px figcaption@
figure@

@figure
  @img |src assets/downloads.svg| |alt Chart, full width| |size full|
  @figcaption size full — 100% figcaption@
figure@

@h2 Image beside text h2@
~ @row is an invisible flex band; each @col is a block placed side by side.
~ Lock the chart to a fixed column, let the prose fill the rest — no floats,
~ nothing to clear. The image fills its column automatically.
@row
  @col |size 260|
    @img |src assets/downloads.svg| |alt Downloads chart|
  col@
  @col
    macOS leads this cycle, with Linux close behind and Windows growing
    fastest. The chart is locked to a 260px column on the left while this
    commentary fills the remaining width — placed side by side without a
    single float or clear.
  col@
row@
